-- akn:att_6__hc_1/p1 akn:att_6__hc_1/p2 akn:att_6__hc_1/p3 akn:att_6__hc_1/p4 akn:att_6__hc_1/p5 akn:att_6__hc_1/p6 akn:att_6__hc_1/p7 akn:att_6__hc_1/p8 akn:att_6__hc_1/p9 akn:att_6__hc_1/p10 akn:att_6__hc_1/p11 akn:att_6__hc_1/p12 akn:att_6__hc_1/p13 akn:att_6__hc_1/p14 akn:att_6__hc_1/p15 akn:att_6__hc_1/p16 akn:att_6__hc_1/p17 akn:att_6__hc_1/p18 akn:att_6__hc_1/p19 akn:att_6__hc_1/p20 akn:att_6__hc_1/p21 akn:att_6__hc_1/p22 Annex ו, the addresses for enquiries (districts, the national service centre, the Ofek centre, promotion, commitment letters, employment approvals, profile); no rule.

-- Examples and checks.

-- 4.1.2's table: every row adds up to the cluster manager's 34 hours.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD r's `frontal or enrichment hours` PLUS r's `management hours` EQUALS r's `cluster hours in all`) `the cluster manager's table`
-- 4.2: 26 + 3 + 7 = 36.
#ASSERT `health frontal hours` PLUS `health individual hours` PLUS `health stay hours` EQUALS `the health-profession week`
-- 4.1.1 and 8: each base is the under-50 base less the age hours.
#ASSERT `the position base` `kindergarten manager` `55 and over, existing` EQUALS 30.4 MINUS `age hours for a full position` 56 TRUE
#ASSERT `the position base` `fellow kindergarten teacher` `55 and over, new` EQUALS 33.8 MINUS `age hours for a full position` 56 FALSE
-- 4.1.4: 7:55 to 14:00 is 6 hours 5 minutes, 6.08 to two places.
#ASSERT ROUND ((605 DIVIDED BY 60) TIMES 100) EQUALS 1008

#ASSERT `the position` 30.4 30.4 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the kindergarten management reward` 0.17 8000 1 EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `the kindergarten management reward` 0.2 10000 1 EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `the advance rate` `academic kindergarten teacher` EQUALS 0.16
#ASSERT `the Ofek Hadash advance` `intern` 10000 0.5 EQUALS 700
#ASSERT `the fellow teacher's supplement` 10000 1.2 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the mentor's rate` 4 EQUALS 0.072
#ASSERT `a mother's position` 1 TRUE EQUALS 1.1
#ASSERT `activity hours paid` 50 EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `the internship counts for` `tenure`
#ASSERT NOT `the internship counts for` `salary seniority`

-- F-2024-25_tashpah_02-a, -b: the forms of annexes ג and ד close on
-- 30.8.2024 (day 26), the body's rules on 31.12.2024 (day 149). The
-- reading adopted: the body's 31.12.2024, which the rules above use.
`annex ג's last day contradicts 3.2.1's` MEANS
    NOT `the forms' last day` EQUALS `the last day for exceptional-joining requests by 3.2.1`
#ASSERT `annex ג's last day contradicts 3.2.1's`

`annex ד's last day contradicts 3.6.5's` MEANS
    NOT `the forms' last day` EQUALS `the last day for requests not to join by 3.6.5`
#ASSERT `annex ד's last day contradicts 3.6.5's`

-- F-2024-25_tashpah_02-c: 2.1.1(5) and (9) send the advance to section 12,
-- which is the management reward; the advance is section 17. The reading
-- adopted: section 17.
`2.1.1 sends the advance to the wrong section` MEANS
    NOT `the section the advance is said to be in` EQUALS `the section the advance is in`
#ASSERT `2.1.1 sends the advance to the wrong section`

-- F-2024-25_tashpah_02-d: 3.2.1 sends promotion of the uncertified to
-- 12.2.2, a number the circular does not have; the rule is 11.2.2. The
-- reading adopted: 11.2.2.
`the numbers the circular gives under 12` MEANS LIST "12.1", "12.1.1", "12.1.2", "12.2"
`3.2.1 cites a section that is not there` MEANS
        (NOT elem `the section 3.2.1 sends promotion to` `the numbers the circular gives under 12`)
    AND (NOT `the section 3.2.1 sends promotion to` EQUALS `the section promotion of the uncertified is in`)
#ASSERT `3.2.1 cites a section that is not there`

-- F-2024-25_tashpah_02-e: 4.1.1's note sends age hours to section 7 (the
-- teaching mother); they are section 8. The reading adopted: section 8.
`4.1.1 sends age hours to the wrong section` MEANS
    NOT `the section age hours are said to be in` EQUALS `the section age hours are in`
#ASSERT `4.1.1 sends age hours to the wrong section`

-- F-2024-25_tashpah_02-f: annex ח is cited and the annexes run א to ו.
-- The reading adopted: annex ו, the circular's list of addresses.
`the circular cites an annex it does not have` MEANS
    NOT elem `the annex the districts' contacts are said to be in` `the annexes the circular has`
#ASSERT `the circular cites an annex it does not have`

-- F-2024-25_tashpah_02-g: 8.2's partial reduction for a part-time
-- teacher has no rule below to compute it. The reading adopted: none is
-- invented; the share of the reduction is an input.
`8.2's partial reduction has no rule` MEANS
    NOT `8.3-8.5 say how a part-time reduction is computed`
#ASSERT `8.2's partial reduction has no rule`

-- F-2024-25_tashpah_02-h: at exactly 25 years, 11.2.2 says both "must
-- certify" (up to 25) and "need not" (25 and more).
`11.2.2 gives 25 years two answers` MEANS
    `11.2.2's answers to "must certify before advancing"` 25 EQUALS LIST TRUE, FALSE
#ASSERT `11.2.2 gives 25 years two answers`

-- 12.2's table gives every whole grade from 1 to 9 exactly one rate, and
-- the rule agrees with it.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN g YIELD `the rates the table gives a new manager at grade` g EQUALS LIST (`the rate of a new manager` g))
            (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9)
#ASSERT `is a grade the conversion may set` 2.5 AND (NOT `is a grade the conversion may set` 2.25)

-- F-2024-25_tashpah_02-i: an unqualified teacher in special education is
-- given 5.5% and 8.5%.
`15 gives an unqualified special-education teacher two rates` MEANS
    `the rates 15 gives an unqualified teacher` TRUE EQUALS LIST 0.055, 0.085
#ASSERT `15 gives an unqualified special-education teacher two rates`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `annex hours worked of row` n IS
    sum (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `annex hours worked`) (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `annex serial` EQUALS n) `annex ה`))

-- F-2024-25_tashpah_02-j: annex ה row 4 has the fellow teacher work five
-- days of 6.08 hours, "in fact 30.8 hours", at "up to 90%": five days of
-- 6.08 are 30.4 hours, which is the 90% (30.4/33.8); 30.8 would be 91.1%.
-- The reading adopted: the rule of 4.1.4-4.1.5 (5 × 6.08 = 30.4 hours, 90%).
`annex ה row 4 counts 5 × 6.08 as 30.8` MEANS
        (NOT 5 TIMES `working hours of a day closing at 14:00` EQUALS 30.8)
    AND 5 TIMES `working hours of a day closing at 14:00` EQUALS 30.4
    AND ROUND (`the position` 30.4 33.8 TIMES 100) EQUALS 90
    AND (NOT ROUND (`the position` 30.8 33.8 TIMES 100) EQUALS 90)
    AND `annex hours worked of row` 4 EQUALS 30.8
#ASSERT `annex ה row 4 counts 5 × 6.08 as 30.8`

-- F-2024-25_tashpah_02-k: rows with the same post, base and schedule state
-- different positions — rows 7 and 9 (a manager on 28.4: 107 and 100),
-- rows 10 and 12 (a fellow teacher on 31.8: 90 and 95.5).
-- The reading adopted: the position is computed by 4.1.5 from the hours
-- actually worked; the annex's position column is not a rule.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `annex position of row` n IS
    sum (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `annex position`) (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `annex serial` EQUALS n) `annex ה`))

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `annex base of row` n IS
    sum (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `annex base`) (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `annex serial` EQUALS n) `annex ה`))

`annex ה states two positions for one base` MEANS
        `annex base of row` 7 EQUALS `annex base of row` 9
    AND (NOT `annex position of row` 7 EQUALS `annex position of row` 9)
    AND `annex base of row` 10 EQUALS `annex base of row` 12
    AND (NOT `annex position of row` 10 EQUALS `annex position of row` 12)
#ASSERT `annex ה states two positions for one base`

#TRACE `the commitment letter is sent by 30.8.2024` 3 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `send the commitment letter` 3 AT 20
#TRACE `no more than 42 weekly hours` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `employ above 42 weekly hours` 44 AT 30
#TRACE `the owner pays the advance monthly` `academic kindergarten teacher` 10000 1 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `pay the Ofek Hadash advance` 1600 AT 28
